commit 3e978558404df4ad1bbb0a5634a03df2b0f9dfa5
Author: Alazer Manakelew <alazermanakelewb@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 13 18:42:57 2026 -0400

    support for spark-tts (#261)
    
    * feat(spark): scaffold Spark-TTS — config, prompt, and BiCodec quantizer/feat-coders/wave-generator
    
    WIP port of Spark-TTS (SparkAudio). Reuses MLXLLM Qwen2 backbone, VocosBackbone,
    WeightNormedConv, and Descript DAC primitives. Config + prompt builder + BiCodec
    quantizer, feat encoder/decoder, and wave generator compile against MLXAudioTTS.
    Remaining: speaker encoder (ECAPA+Perceiver+FSQ), BiCodec orchestrator (mel +
    wav2vec2), and the SparkModel generate loop.
    
    * feat(spark): add BiCodec speaker-encoder detokenize (FSQ decode + project)
    
    * feat(spark): complete + numerically validate BiCodec detokenize
    
    BiCodec synthesis path (quantizer, FSQ speaker decode, AdaLayerNorm prenet,
    HiFiGAN wave generator) ported and validated against the Python reference on
    mlx-community/Spark-TTS-0.5B-bf16: 322/322 weight keys match, output relative
    error 0.0009 vs the reference waveform. Shape-guided sanitize handles the
    standard/transpose conv weight layouts.
    
    * feat(spark): add Spark-TTS controllable synthesis (Qwen2 + BiCodec)
    
    End-to-end MLX Swift port of Spark-TTS controllable TTS: a Qwen2 LM (reused from
    MLXLLM) emits BiCodec semantic/global tokens decoded by the ported BiCodec
    (quantizer, FSQ speaker decode, AdaLayerNorm prenet, HiFiGAN wave generator).
    Registered in the TTS factory (disambiguating the generic qwen2 config by repo
    name). BiCodec validated numerically vs the Python reference (~0.09% rel. error);
    end-to-end smoke test synthesizes audio via TTS.loadModel. Voice cloning
    (reference-audio encode) is not yet included.
    
    * refactor(spark): remove unshipped encode-path dead code
    
    Drop the unused encode path to keep only the validated synthesis path: remove
    SparkConfiguration (LM config now from MLXLLM Qwen2Configuration), SparkFeatEncoder,
    the quantizer tokenize/in_project, and the voice-cloning prompt builder. Trim the
    BiCodec config to the decode subset. Codec numerics unchanged (0.09% rel error);
    e2e still synthesizes audio.
    
    * style(spark): drop file-header and inline comments, keep docstrings
    
    * feat(spark): add BiCodec mel-spectrogram for reference-audio encoding
    
    Slaney mel-spectrogram (STFT + hann window + slaney filterbank) matching the
    Python BiCodec tokenizer, used to derive speaker/global tokens from a reference
    clip. Adds the MLXFFT product dependency to the TTS target.
    
    * feat(spark): add FVQ encode (in_project + cosine tokenize)
    
    Adds the factorized vector quantizer's encode path: in_project plus L2-normalized
    cosine-distance nearest-codebook lookup, producing semantic token ids from encoder
    latents. Stops dropping quantizer.in_project weights in the BiCodec sanitizer.
    
    * feat(spark): add BiCodec feature encoder + semantic tokenize
    
    Ports the feature encoder (Vocos backbone + downsample stages + linear projection)
    and BiCodec.tokenizeSemantic, mapping wav2vec2 features to semantic token ids.
    Adds the encoder config and stops dropping encoder weights in the sanitizer.
    
    * feat(spark): add Wav2Vec2-large-xlsr-53 feature extractor
    
    Ports the xlsr-53 encoder (7-layer conv feature extractor, feature projection,
    weight-normed positional conv, 24 stable-layer-norm transformer layers) and
    returns the layer 11/14/16 hidden-state mix the BiCodec tokenizer consumes.
    Runs deterministically (no dropout), matching the Python reference in eval mode.
    
    * feat(spark): add ECAPA-TDNN latent trunk for the speaker encoder
    
    Ports the ECAPA-TDNN feature trunk (Conv1dReluBn, SE-Res2 blocks, 1x1 aggregation)
    that produces the 1536-d latent the speaker tokenizer consumes; the pooling head
    is omitted since tokenization only needs the latent. Loads under eval mode for
    BatchNorm running stats. Matches the reference exactly.
    
    * feat(spark): add perceiver resampler + FSQ encode for global tokens
    
    Ports the Perceiver resampler (learned latent cross-attention over the ECAPA
    feature map) and the residual FSQ encode path (bound/round/index), yielding the
    32 global speaker tokens. Re-keys the perceiver layer weights and stops dropping
    the perceiver/FSQ-project-in weights in the sanitizer. Global tokens match the
    reference exactly.
    
    * feat(spark): wire up reference-audio voice cloning
    
    Adds the reference-audio path to SparkModel.generate: tokenize the reference clip
    into global speaker tokens (mel -> ECAPA -> perceiver -> FSQ) and, when a reference
    transcript is given, semantic tokens (Wav2Vec2 -> encoder -> FVQ); build the
    voice-clone prompt and detokenize with the reference speaker tokens. Wav2Vec2 is
    loaded lazily and only when a reference transcript is supplied.
    
    Validated end-to-end against mlx-audio: global tokens and the clone prompt match
    exactly, and cloning synthesizes speech in the reference voice.

