commit 3506fb93cc3b9e4a642079d5384eaca0373962e6
Author: Kn0688 <128996369+Kn0688@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 31 23:40:08 2026 +0800

    FireRedASR2: fix beam search topK gathering across rows (#253)
    
    The 2D branch of topK used plain `take`, which broadcasts the
    flattened indices across every row: with beam > 1 all candidate tokens
    were scored with beam 0's logits. Use `takeAlong` so each index row
    gathers from the matching input row.
    
    Adds characterization tests pinning topK semantics and the toy-model
    beam search output (pre-fix output was [3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4]).
    
    Co-authored-by: feiguodong1 <feiguodong1@jd.com>

diff --git a/Sources/MLXAudioSTT/Models/FireRedASR2/FireRedASR2Model.swift b/Sources/MLXAudioSTT/Models/FireRedASR2/FireRedASR2Model.swift
