commit cae704f53bc32a3d0b606823828fbc5bedaaf388
Author: SAP Sentinel <69308174+SAPSentinel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 16 21:36:27 2026 +0530

    Kokoro: expose the per-phoneme durations generate already computes (#239)
    
    callAsFunction predicts per-phoneme durations on every synthesis and
    returns them as predDur, but generate discards them. Callers doing
    lip-sync, viseme animation or subtitle alignment then have to re-derive
    timing from the waveform, which is strictly less accurate than the
    alignment the model just used to produce it.
    
    generateWithDurations returns (audio, phonemes, durations); generate
    delegates to it and is unchanged for existing callers.
    
    The phonemized string is returned alongside the durations because
    durations alone cannot be mapped back to phonemes — generate already
    computes it internally and drops it too.
    
    Co-authored-by: Sarvesh Kandala <sarvesh.ak@icloud.com>

