commit c5d40544f0efd76849415098617cac13055e16c0
Author: marcoIannello <148067382+iannellomarco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 23 00:34:09 2026 +0200

    Quantized KV cache for MOSS-Transcribe-Diarize (opt-in, memory-bounded long-form) (#225)
    
    * Inject MOSS audio features for any KVCache type on prefill
    
    The gate downcast to KVCacheSimple, so a quantized or otherwise
    non-simple cache silently skipped audio-feature injection. Use the
    protocol-level offset instead.
    
    * Thread optional KV-cache quantization through MOSS generation
    
    STTGenerateParameters gains kvBits/kvGroupSize/quantizedKVStart and
    MOSS generateTokenIds calls maybeQuantizeKVCache after the prompt is
    prefilled, so prefill runs at model precision and only the retained
    context is quantized. kvBits == nil (the default) leaves every code
    path bit-for-bit identical to before.
    
    * Load pre-quantized MOSS checkpoints
    
    sanitize already detected .scales keys but fromModelDirectory never
    swapped modules to their quantized variants, so a quantized repo
    failed to load. Decode quantization/quantization_config from
    config.json and apply quantize(model:) gated on the presence of
    scales tensors, mirroring the Canary and Qwen3ASR loaders.
    
    * Update mlx-swift to 0.31.4 and mlx-swift-lm to 3.31.4
    
    * Test quantization config decoding and KV parameter defaults
    
    * Quantize the MOSS KV cache during chunked prefill
    
    Quantizing only after the full prompt was prefilled held the entire
    prompt's full-precision KV as a transient peak - for an hour-long
    meeting that peak alone exceeds a small machine's memory, defeating
    the point of cache quantization. Match mlx-lm and quantize inside
    the chunked prompt loop instead, so the retained context is
    compressed as prefill progresses.
    
    Multi-token steps over a quantized cache need an additive float
    mask: the quantized attention path substitutes a near-zero constant
    (not -inf) for masked positions of symbolic/boolean masks, letting
    future positions leak through the softmax. Supply the exact additive
    mask for that case; every other path is unchanged. kvBits == nil
    remains bit-for-bit identical to prior behavior.
    
    * Bound the quantized-prefill memory spike with a smaller chunk
    
    The quantized attention path materializes its score tensor, so each
    prefill chunk transiently allocates chunk x context x heads floats -
    at 2048-token chunks over an hour-long prompt that spike reaches
    multiple GB per layer. Quantized decodes now prefill in 512-token
    chunks; the full-precision path is unchanged.
    
    * Trim comments to the essentials per review
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: iannebot <iannebot@users.noreply.github.com>
    Co-authored-by: Prince Canuma <prince.gdt@gmail.com>

