commit 6ea59e549294151256b98b1cdbb346ba946d12d0
Author: Tom Vaucourt <34662901+T0mSIlver@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 20 22:47:41 2026 +0200

    Hoist per-layer-invariant attention inputs out of the Voxtral layer loops (#231)
    
    * Hoist per-layer-invariant attention inputs out of the Voxtral layer loops
    
    Every Voxtral Realtime transformer layer rebuilt identical per-forward
    values inside its attention: the interleaved-RoPE cos/sin tables (encoder
    and decoder), and the SDPA sliding-window mask (encoder). That is
    O(nLayers) copies of the same ~7-15 tiny kernels per forward pass — pure
    launch overhead, and in live streaming (a handful of encoder frames plus
    1-2 decoded tokens every ~100 ms chunk) those launches, not bandwidth,
    dominate step time.
    
    The encoder now builds a shared VoxtralRealtimeEncoderAttentionInputs
    (RoPE tables + mask) once per pass in encodeFull/encodeChunked/
    encodeIncremental; the decoder computes its RoPE tables once per forward
    in VoxtralRealtimeDecoder.callAsFunction. Sharing one mask across encoder
    layers relies on the layer KV-caches advancing in lockstep, which is how
    all three encode paths drive them; the builder asserts it.
    
    No output change: the hoisted values are produced by exactly the same
    operations on the same inputs as the per-layer versions, so every layer
    consumes bit-identical arrays and the temperature-0 token stream is
    unchanged. Covered by the existing offline/streaming equivalence tests.
    
    * Tighten the encoder lockstep precondition to nil-ness uniformity
    
    A present-but-empty cache selects the explicit-array mask branch while a
    nil cache can take .causal, so sharing one mask also requires uniform
    nil-ness across layers. No in-repo caller mixes them; the precondition now
    makes the bit-identical claim hold unconditionally. Also scope the decoder
    ropeFrequencies helper to the file (its only call site) and document the
    per-chunk rebuild in encodeChunked and the mask-dtype assumption.
    
    * Tighten the hoisted-attention-input comments

