commit 3cfa97201572e438eece2036299383834473253f
Author: JacobLinCool <jacoblincool@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jun 28 07:41:18 2026 +0800

    Add OmniVoice TTS (NAR diffusion over Qwen3 + HiggsAudioV2 codec, with voice cloning) (#209)
    
    * Qwen3 (TTS): rebase backbone on mlx-swift-lm implementation
    
    Replace the custom Qwen3 implementation with the verified mlx-swift-lm
    version: namespaced module classes (Qwen3Attention/Qwen3MLP/...),
    simplified config decoding with defaults, and an embeddings-level API
    (getEmbeddings/forwardWithEmbeddings) so non-autoregressive models can
    drive the backbone with mixed text/audio embeddings.
    
    * Add OmniVoice TTS (NAR diffusion over Qwen3 + HiggsAudioV2 codec)
    
    Multilingual zero-shot TTS: auto-voice and instruction-based voice design
    modes, iterative-unmask generation with classifier-free guidance matching
    the Python mlx-audio reference (bidirectional attention, cosine-shifted
    timestep schedule, <|denoise|> emitted only with reference audio, numStep
    clamped >= 1). Supports both split and fused checkpoint layouts; the
    HiggsAudioV2 semantic encode path (voice cloning) is not ported yet and
    its weights are dropped at load time — see Models/OmniVoice/README.md.
    
    Verified against the Python implementation: tokenizer ids identical,
    forward logits parity (argmax agreement 99.9%), codec decode sample-exact
    (corr 1.0 at a constant 25-sample offset), TTS->ASR round trip exact.
    
    * OmniVoice: honor requested duration in target token estimation
    
    duration_s was accepted by the API surface but never read by the token
    estimator; auto-duration also over-allocated English ~2x via the
    chars*4 heuristic. Port the Python RuleDurationEstimator (phonetic
    weights + low-duration boost) and map duration to ceil(duration*25).
    
    * ModelUtils: validate model snapshots recursively
    
    resolveOrDownloadModel only looked at the top level of a snapshot when
    checking for the required extension and config.json, which broke repos
    that keep weights in version subfolders (e.g. DeepFilterNet-mlx
    v1/v2/v3): files downloaded fine but validation reported
    incompleteDownload and cleared the cache.
    
    * OmniVoice: implement the HiggsAudioV2 semantic encode path (voice cloning)
    
    Port the full HiggsAudioTokenizer.encode pipeline from the Python
    mlx-audio reference:
    
    - OmniVoiceSemantic.swift: HuBERT (semantic_model.*) with group-norm
      feature extractor, weight-normed positional conv embedding, and
      post-norm transformer layers averaged over all hidden states;
      SemanticEncoder CNN (encoder_semantic.*); torchaudio-parity
      Hann-windowed sinc resampling (AVAudioConverter does not match).
    - encode() now fuses [acoustic | semantic] features through fc and
      residual-quantizes, replacing the acoustic-only fc2-inversion
      approximation.
    - Fix OmniVoiceRVQQuantizer encode: each stage must quantize the
      residual left by previous stages, not the original input (parity
      with ResidualVectorQuantizer.encode).
    - sanitize: keep semantic_model./encoder_semantic./fc weights, remap
      parametrized weight-norm keys to weight_g/weight_v.
    - Semantic modules are only built when the checkpoint ships them
      (mlx-community/OmniVoice does; the bf16 variant is stripped) and
      encode() reports a clear error otherwise.
    
    Verified against the Python reference on identical 8s input:
    199/200 RVQ frames identical end-to-end (the 2 root flips are
    near-tie argmins, relative distance gaps 4.6e-4 / 1.2e-3, with one
    legitimate downstream cascade); cloned audio MFCC-timbre similarity
    to the Python clone of the same prompt: 0.994.
    
    * OmniVoice: style cleanup, dead-code removal, and doc fixes
    
    - Rename `snakeAlpha` -> `SnakeAlpha` and `res_unit{1,2,3}` -> `resUnit{1,2,3}`
      (via `@ModuleInfo(key:)` so checkpoint weight keys are unchanged) to match
      the repo's PascalCase-type / camelCase-property conventions.
    - Remove dead code: unused `makeCausalMask`, `normalizedCodebookWeights`,
      an unused loop binding, and an empty MARK; strip trailing whitespace.
    - Silence warnings in the new code: unused `guard let tokenizer`, a redundant
      `try`, and the `.none` Optional ambiguity in the attention path (pass `nil`).
    - Qwen3: drop a dead local in the transformer block and normalize range-operator
      spacing to the repo-dominant unspaced form.
    - Qwen3 Config: make `maxPositionEmbeddings` a constructor parameter instead of
      a hardcoded value (field is never read at inference; no behavior change).
    - Docs: correct the OmniVoice README (voice cloning works; 9 RVQ codebooks) and
      add OmniVoice to the root README's TTS model table and list.
    
    * OmniVoice: restore Qwen3 backbone doc/inline comments
    
    Address PR #209 review: the mlx-swift-lm rebase stripped the explanatory
    comments from the TTS-specific paths (decode/encode/parse/prepareInputIds/
    generate/generateStream/load). Restore them; no logic changes.
    
    * Revert unrelated ModelUtils recursive snapshot search
    
    Address PR #209 review: the recursive firstNonEmptyFile change was brought
    in accidentally while testing and isn't needed for OmniVoice (both repos
    keep config.json / model.safetensors at the top level). Restore main's
    top-level lookup.
    
    * OmniVoice: clarify bf16 audio codec wording in README
    
    Address PR #209 review: it's the audio codec (audio_tokenizer/), not the
    text tokenizer, that the bf16 repo ships without the semantic encode path;
    the layout difference is unrelated to quantization.

